  "description": "KACJOR crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H76 Dy6 N12 O21,8.75(C1 H4 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy12 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.351-4.378 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.80-144.90°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C88H76Dy6N12O21·8.75MeOH·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
